{"lines": ["One last file. And this one is silence from the Bronze Age.", "In 1908, on Crete, the archaeologist Luigi Pernier dug up a disc of fired clay, sixteen centimetres across, in the Minoan palace of Phaistos. Both sides are covered in a spiral of signs. Two hundred and forty-two sign impressions, from forty-five different signs, pressed into soft clay before it was fired.", "At first, some scholars suspected a forgery. Today it is generally accepted as authentic. And nobody has read it. It is not even clear that it is writing.", "And back in California, the Zodiac sent two shorter codes in 1970. Thirteen characters, and thirty-two. Hundreds of solutions have been proposed. Oranchak says it is practically impossible to tell if any of them are correct.", "So here is the honest version. Known: Zodiac's three-hundred-and-forty-character cipher, three Kryptos messages, and Beale's second page have been read. Proposed: Webb, for the Somerton Man; a hoax, for Beale. Unsolved: Voynich, Dorabella, K4, Phaistos, and the two short Zodiac codes.", "Rule seven. Say unknown out loud. Saying it is how the next person knows where to look."], "words": [["One", 0.0, 0.2], ["last", 0.2, 0.42], ["file.", 0.42, 0.88], ["And", 1.3, 1.5], ["this", 1.5, 1.66], ["one", 1.66, 1.92], ["is", 1.92, 2.26], ["silence", 2.26, 2.54], ["from", 2.54, 3.06], ["the", 3.06, 3.16], ["Bronze", 3.16, 3.36], ["Age.", 3.36, 3.9], ["In", 4.82, 4.96], ["1908,", 4.96, 5.58], ["on", 6.12, 6.22], ["Crete,", 6.22, 6.68], ["the", 7.0, 7.16], ["archaeologist", 7.16, 7.86], ["Luigi", 7.86, 8.18], ["Pernier", 8.18, 8.94], ["dug", 8.94, 9.26], ["up", 9.26, 9.44], ["a", 9.44, 9.54], ["disc", 9.54, 9.82], ["of", 9.82, 10.02], ["fired", 10.02, 10.34], ["clay,", 10.34, 10.66], ["sixteen", 10.66, 11.58], ["centimetres", 11.58, 12.3], ["across,", 12.3, 12.58], ["in", 12.58, 13.32], ["the", 13.32, 13.42], ["Minoan", 13.42, 13.72], ["palace", 13.72, 14.16], ["of", 14.16, 14.36], ["Phaistos.", 14.36, 15.54], ["Both", 15